/// Synopsis: covered content that reaches the next page after a `#pause` (a callout, an `emph-box` with a title, a table, a quotation and running text) converges: the callout, the box and the table are veiled whole; the quotation at the foot of the page is hidden, in the same room as when veiled, because the covered text after it goes on to the next page, where it is hidden too (the document did not converge, with a quotation box hidden smaller than veiled). The footer numbers the two pages 1 and 2 on both steps (Touying repeated 2 on the second step). Arrow lines with a `#pause` in a paragraph of its own, which reach the next page, converge, with the same numbers on both steps.
#import "../../common.typ": *
#show: setup
#include "body.typ"
